  "final_text": "All four steps are done.\n\n1. **Data view:** 'Kibana Sample Data Flights' (index `kibana_sample_data_flights`) has 33 fields. Its time field is `timestamp`.\n2. **Dashboard:** I created 'S4-3ec7c5f2 Flights' on that data view with exactly two panels. One is a line chart of flights over time, and the other is a bar chart of flights by `Carrier` (top 10).\n3. **Alert rule:** I created 'S4-3ec7c5f2 Cancelled flights' as an index-threshold rule. It runs every minute and fires when the count of documents matching `Cancelled: true` is above 10 in a 5-minute window. I created it with `enabled: true`, so it didn't need enabling afterwards. It has no actions attached.\n4. **Edit and read-back:** I renamed the carrier panel to 'Flights by carrier', and the dashboard now shows both panel titles. Reading the rule back shows `enabled: true`, and its last run had status `ok`.\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes",
